{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/focusmode_top

    What the top of the body carries on an activity page that can switch focus mode in place.

    The theme's core renderer appends it to core's standard top of body html, which Boost Union's
    layout template prints first inside the page wrapper, so it follows core's skip link and comes
    before Boost Union's navbar.

    The bar is always in the page and the stylesheet shows it only under the focus mode body class.
    The status line is NOT inside it on purpose: a live region inside an element that is not
    displayed announces nothing, and the module writes the new mode here on every switch, in both
    directions. It starts empty, so the first paint announces nothing.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a Mustache
    comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * bar - the bar sub-context, documented in the focusmode_bar template

    Example context (json):
    {
        "bar": {
            "navbarcolorclasses": "navbar-dark bg-primary",
            "coursename": "APH-2026",
            "closeurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=2#module-4",
            "title": "Vital signs",
            "headeractions": [],
            "expanded": false,
            "widthlabel": "Wide reading column",
            "hasmore": false,
            "moreitems": [],
            "editswitch": "",
            "leaveform": true,
            "actionurl": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/focus.php",
            "sesskey": "AbC123dEf4",
            "cmid": 4,
            "closelabel": "Exit focus mode",
            "closetitle": "Back to the ordinary page"
        }
    }
}}
<div class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-region="dimensions-focus-status"></div>
{{#bar}}
    {{> theme_dimensions/focusmode_bar }}
{{/bar}}
